                "text" : "Approach Speeds:"
              },
              {
                "text" : "Fly no less than on-speed AOA (amber donut)—cross-check with airspeed to avoid going slow."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Aircraft Handling:"
              },
              {
                "text" : "Heavier aircraft are less responsive to pitch and power inputs."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Sink rates increase faster—anticipate and counteract with coordinated power and trim."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Flare & Touchdown:"
              },
              {
                "text" : "Flare should be more gradual and extended—aircraft will settle faster."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Avoid excessive pitch-up."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Touch down on-speed and on aimpoint—do not float or land long."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Know the entry airspeed, altitude, configuration, and cockpit setup before you start the maneuver."
              },
              {
                "text" : "Standards \/ numbers"
